          %h3#exceptional_geometry Exceptional geometry
          %p
            For the moment see the remarks/references on supergravity at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+geometry"} exceptional geometry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+geometry"} exceptional generalized geometry
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            is that for supergravity Lagrangians “of ordinary type” it turns out that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
          %p is the highest dimension possible, but see also at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/12-dimensional+supergravity"} 12-dimensional supergravity
          %p for some qualification.
          %p
            All lower dimensional theories in this class appear as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            of this theory or are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformations"} deformations
            of such:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-dimensional+supergravity"} 10-dimensional supergravity
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} massive type IIA supergravity
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+supergravity"} type IIB supergravity
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/9-dimensional+supergravity"} 9-dimensional supergravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-dimensional+supergravity"} 8-dimensional supergravity
            %li
              %p
