                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "supersymmetry#ReferencesHistory"} supersymmetry – History
              \.
          %h3#related Related
          %p Further physics monographs on supergravity include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                I. L. Buchbinder, S. M. Kuzenko,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ideas and methods of supersymmetry and supergravity; or A walk through superspace
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.com/books?isbn=0750305061"} googB
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julius+Wess"}> Julius Wess
                , Jonathan Bagger,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and supergravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum theory of fields
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.springer.com/gp/book/9781402013386"}> Concise Encyclopedia of Supersymmetry, S. Duplij, J. Bagger, W. Siegel (Eds.), Springer, 2004
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://ivv5hpp.uni-muenster.de/u/douplii/susy/SUSYEnc_Story.pdf"} SUSY story
                narrated by its founders
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+problem"} Cauchy problem
            for classical solutions of simple supergravity has been discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yvonne+Choquet-Bruhat"}> Yvonne Choquet-Bruhat
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Cauchy+Problem+in+Classical+Supergravity"} The Cauchy Problem in Classical Supergravity
          %p
            A canonical textbook reference for the role of Calabi-Yau manifolds in compactifications of 10-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            is volume II, starting on page 1091 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.+Deligne"}> P. Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/P.+Etingof"} P. Etingof
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Freed"} D. Freed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Kazhdan"} D. Kazhdan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Witten"} E. Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                  , A course for mathematicians
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
          %p
            Discussion of solutions with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 1
            global supersymmetry left and their relation to Calabi-Yau compactifications are for instance in
          %ul
            %li#GMPT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mariana+Gra%C3%B1a"}> Mariana Graña
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ruben+Minasian"} Ruben Minasian
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Tomasiello"} Alessandro Tomasiello
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Generalized structures of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                  vacua
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0505212"} arXiv:hep-th/0505212
          %h3#PhenomenologyReferences Phenomenology
          %p
            On supergravity
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
          %h4#dark_matter Dark matter
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"} dark matter
            candidate:
          %ul
            %li#EllisOlive10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Ellis"}> John Ellis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keith+Olive"} Keith Olive
              %em Supersymmetric Dark Matter Candidates
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.3651"}> arXiv:1001.3651
              )
          %p#NicolaiMeissner
            A proposal for super-heavy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitinos"} gravitinos
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"} dark matter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D8+supergravity"} D=4 N=8 supergravity
            into
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E10"} E10
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %ul
            %li#MeissnerNicolai18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Standard Model Fermions and Infinite-Dimensional R-Symmetries
                %strong 121
                091601 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.09606"}> arXiv:1804.09606
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.121.091601"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.121.091601
            %li#MeissnerNicolai18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Planck Mass Charged Gravitino Dark Matter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.01441"} arXiv:1809.01441
          %p following the proposal towards the end of
          %ul
            %li#GellMann83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Murray+Gell-Mann"}> Murray Gell-Mann
                , introductory talk at
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelter_Island_Conference"} Shelter Island II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Gell-Mann_ShelterIslandII_1983.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                in:
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Shelter Island II: Proceedings of the 1983 Shelter Island Conference on Quantum Field Theory and the Fundamental Problems of Physics
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                %em Supermassive gravitinos and giant primordial black holes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.11889"}> arXiv:2007.11889
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"}> Krzysztof A. Meissner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                %em
                  Evidence for a stable supermassive gravitino with charge
                  = succeed "?" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2/3
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.09131"}> arXiv:2303.09131
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Adrianna Kruk, Michał Lesiuk,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+A.+Meissner"} Krzysztof A. Meissner
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                %em Signatures of supermassive charged gravitinos in liquid scintillator detectors
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.04883"}> arXiv:2407.04883
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#dark_energy Dark energy
          %p
            On supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            in relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+energy"} dark energy
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
          %ul
            %li
              Y. Aghababaie,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cliff+P.+Burgess"} Cliff P. Burgess
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Quevedo"} Fernando Quevedo
              = succeed "," do
                %em Towards a Naturally Small Cosmological Constant from Branes in 6D Supergravity
              %strong 680
              (2004) 389-414 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0304256"}> arXiv:hep-th/0304256
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.12.015"} doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2003.12.015
          %h4#cosmic_inflation Cosmic inflation
          %p
            On supergravity in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+inflation"} cosmic inflation
          %ul
            %li#DalianisFarakos15
              Ioannis Dalianis,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fotis+Farakos"} Fotis Farakos
              %em
                On the initial conditions for inflation with plateau potentials: the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi R
